sub:assertion {
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-delphi10000-gasterosteus-aculeatus-benthic-turing-wavelength-s0> pk:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-gasterosteus-aculeatus-benthic-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> .
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-gasterosteus-aculeatus-benthic-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Benthic stickleback cellular Turing wavelength (43 µm, Holocene 0 Ma) — MorphoEval overall 82.8/100" ;
        dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
        dct:description "Pass 1 reproduction of Schnakenberg kinetics on a 32^2 dermal patch whose grid spacing makes the linear critical wavelength 43.15 µm (4.315e-05 m) at 0 Ma. The marine predecessor's organ-scale bar is 2.4 mm at 0.015 Ma; the benthic organ-scale sibling is 2.2 mm. This slot does not reuse those parameters. Self-test reported Pearson r = 0.9846, RMSE = 5.97 gray levels, KS D = 0.175, nonlinear crest-to-trough 20.24 µm against λ_c/2 = 21.575 µm. Overall 82.8/100 (faithfulness 81.3, reproducibility 86.3); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 0c76d15d14afcec6c366e1b9274a6586a0de48fc; environment: . Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 80, Morphological realism / specimen match 82, Parameter expressivity 84, Morphometric validation 80, Source and data traceability 90, Code-to-model traceability 82, Reproducibility package 86. Output judged: docs/media/gasterosteus_aculeatus_benthic_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png: rendered output of models/2026-delphi10000-gasterosteus-aculeatus-benthic-turing-wavelength-s0.py at 0c76d15d14afcec6c366e1b9274a6586a0de48fc, image/png, 471783 B, 1512×984 px, artifact_sha256 7a7bb5162dedf098a96ab87f18cf8648c80f4b41b3f220e1290be8a2118014b9 (sha256 7a7bb5162dedf098a96ab87f18cf8648c80f4b41b3f220e1290be8a2118014b9), spec_fingerprint 6cbd39d1eecf1ced91a3e8503e825e2dd31d3fa2253d092c63bf2c4eb19fc08a. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: 6cbd39d1eecf1ced91a3e8503e825e2dd31d3fa2253d092c63bf2c4eb19fc08a; artifact_sha256: 7a7bb5162dedf098a96ab87f18cf8648c80f4b41b3f220e1290be8a2118014b9. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Low-plate Eda alleles and Pitx1 pelvic-enhancer deletion distinguish post-glacial benthic sticklebacks from the complete-plate marine ancestor (Colosimo 2005; Chan 2010). | Juvenile pigment patterns in threespine sticklebacks are genetically divergent (Greenwood et al. 2011); Kit ligand dosage changes pigmentation (Miller et al. 2007). | Turing 1952 and Schnakenberg 1979 define k_c. Kondo and Asai 1995 and Nakamasu et al. 2009 show activator-inhibitor chromatophore patterns in other teleosts.; reconstructed_in_script: Schnakenberg integration with a=0.1, b=0.9, gamma=0.3, Du=0.55, Dv=12, seed 3234, and dx chosen so linear λ_c = 43.15 µm. | Azimuthal luminance of the canonical detail plate fit by c0 + c1 U(r) + c2 V(r).; transfer_boundary: Zebrafish and angelfish rate constants are not benthic-stickleback measurements. | 43 µm is the catalog detail-tier assignment, not a published melanophore count on G. aculeatus.; does_not_claim: Does not claim the Commons lateral photograph (Ron Offermans, CC BY-SA 3.0) is a benthic low-plate fish. | Does not claim the gallery detail plate is a raw 43 µm lattice micrograph. | Does not claim the 2.2 mm organ-scale benthic model.." ;
        dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
        pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
        pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
        pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: Animate the GIF from Schnakenberg snapshots passed through the steady readout, and keep the last frame equal to the fitted profile.",
            "remediation needed: Inset the CC BY-SA Commons voucher on the comparison figure and state that it is not the 43 µm target.",
            "remediation needed: Integrate every amplitude seed for the full 9000 steps and report the coefficient of variation.",
            "remediation needed: Report the activator-only radial correlation with no fitted inhibitor gain, next to the two-field Pearson r." ;
        pk:hasScore "0.828"^^xsd:double ;
        pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> a pk:Model ;
        rdfs:label "Grok 4.7 (builder-assessor, pass 1)" ;
        dct:identifier "grok-4.7" ;
        prov:actedOnBehalfOf <https://w3id.org/probknow/agent/morphoeval-loop-3234> .
}

